.8x net debt to EBITDA ($1.0B of cash against $1.2B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.3x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.37 in the distress zone.","The value-trap profile is elevated (61/100); see the breakdown below."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 8.2% over 3 years, 25.6% over 5 years and 2.4% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 28%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Margins are contracting (-2.8% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 13%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 4.3% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 29, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.4%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 10.9% a year to shareholders (10.9% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.3% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 37.1% of the float, 12.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 2,455 employees, each generates about $770K of revenue, 2.0x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 8.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $66K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.9M (2x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $44K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":52,"head":"Avoid: Altman Z in the distress zone (1.37).","pros":["Trades 58% below fair value of $16.51","Revenue grew 25.6%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.8x","P/E 9.0x vs sector 17.7x","P/FCF 5.1x vs sector 15.8x"],"cons":["ROIC 6.8% vs WACC 7.0%","Interest coverage only 1.3x","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.37)","EV/EBITDA 13.6x vs sector 10.5x","12-1 month momentum -29%"],"flags":["Altman Z in the distress zone (1.37)","Operating income covers interest only 1.3x"],"need":[],"buy_below":14